Table full name: bigquery-public-data.covid19_nyt.excess_deaths
Column name: country Type: STRING Description: The country reported
Column name: placename Type: STRING Description: The place in the country reported
Column name: frequency Type: STRING Description: Weekly or monthly, depending on how the data is recorded
Column name: start_date Type: DATE Description: The first date included in the period
Column name: end_date Type: DATE Description: The last date included in the period
Column name: year Type: STRING Description: Year reported
Column name: month Type: INT64 Description: Numerical month
Column name: week Type: INT64 Description: Epidemiological week, which is a standardized way of counting weeks to allow for year-over-year comparisons. Most countries start epi weeks on Mondays, but others vary
Column name: deaths Type: INT64 Description: The total number of confirmed deaths recorded from any cause
Column name: expected_deaths Type: INT64 Description: The baseline number of expected deaths, calculated from a historical average
Column name: excess_deaths Type: INT64 Description: The number of deaths minus the expected deaths
Column name: baseline Type: STRING Description: The years used to calculate expected_deaths
